{"id":55571,"ord":23,"n_segments":90,"prev":55570,"next":55572,"doc":{"id":"68090","title":"68090_Ed Garland oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Ed Garland","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68090/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68090"},"chapter":"From New Orleans to Chicago","title":"Freddie Keppard and Garland's own Chicago band","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Keppard joined Garland's Chicago band when Sugar Johnny fell ill; Garland names Palmer, Duke Dewey, Lil Hardin and Tubby Hall, then turned the band over to Dewey.","period":"c. 1918-20","year_from":1918,"year_to":1918,"words":225,"start":[38,6],"end":[40,6],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68090#s55571","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Chicago","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"New York","focus":0,"type":"city"}],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Ed Garland's band","focus":1,"leader":"Ed Garland"}]},"people":[{"name":"Freddie Keppard","qid":"Q490080","n":4},{"name":"Sugar Johnny Dunn","qid":null,"n":4},{"name":"Tubby Hall","qid":"Q1774981","n":3},{"name":"Lil Hardin","qid":"Q462562","n":3},{"name":"Lawrence Duhé","qid":"Q137935","n":2},{"name":"Louis Armstrong","qid":"Q1779","n":1},{"name":"Ed Garland","qid":"Q1282347","n":1},{"name":"May Elaine","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Roy Palmer","qid":"Q1685379","n":1}],"story":{"theme":33,"theme_name":"Chicago: the jazz migration and its clubs","community":59,"community_name":"Going north: working the Chicago jazz scene","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":38,"b":6,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah. That's nice. Okay. You also played with another famous trumpet player, Freddie Keppard."},{"p":38,"b":7,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Freddie Keppard, yeah."},{"p":38,"b":8,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Did you join him in Chicago?"},{"p":38,"b":9,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Huh?"},{"p":38,"b":10,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Did you play with him in Chicago?"},{"p":38,"b":11,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Oh, yeah. When he come to Chicago -- when he come back from New York to come back to Chicago, he was playing with this girl that I went to play with, May Elaine."},{"p":38,"b":12,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":38,"b":13,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And they quit."},{"p":38,"b":14,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"I see."},{"p":38,"b":15,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And he was in New York. He come"},{"p":39,"b":0,"s":"","x":"this man hired Freddie to play with us."},{"p":39,"b":1,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"back to Chicago and (Unintelligible)."},{"p":39,"b":2,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"I see."},{"p":39,"b":3,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"With me, you see. A boy named Sugar Johnny was playing with me trumpet."},{"p":39,"b":4,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Sugar Johnny Dunn?"},{"p":39,"b":5,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Huh?"},{"p":39,"b":6,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Dunn was his last name? Was that Sugar Johnny Dunn?"},{"p":39,"b":7,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Yeah."},{"p":39,"b":8,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh. Yes."},{"p":39,"b":9,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And he's sick now, and Freddie played, you see?"},{"p":39,"b":10,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh. Who else was in that band, Tudi Tootie? Your Chicago band."},{"p":39,"b":11,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"I had Roy Palmer on the trombone."},{"p":39,"b":12,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":39,"b":13,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Louis --"},{"p":39,"b":14,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Who was the clarinet?"},{"p":39,"b":15,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Lawrence Duht Dewey."},{"p":39,"b":16,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":39,"b":17,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Was on the clarinet. And Lil Little played the piano for me."},{"p":39,"b":18,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"That was Lil Little Hardin?"},{"p":39,"b":19,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Lil Little Hardin."},{"p":40,"b":0,"s":"","x":"HEMLOCK ERASABLE COTTON CONTENT"},{"p":40,"b":1,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Right."},{"p":40,"b":2,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And Tubby played the drums."},{"p":40,"b":3,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Tubby Hall."},{"p":40,"b":4,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Tubby Hall."},{"p":40,"b":5,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Right."},{"p":40,"b":6,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And I was on the bass. Because when I left there, I put Lawrence Duke' Dewey -- I turned the band over to Lawrence Duke' Dewey."}]}